WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:00.960
- All right, everybody.

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.490
We've reached the end of the hour,

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.610
but before we go, I have one
last amazing story to share.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.251
This is what I'm liking.
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.251 --> 00:00:09.870
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.610
So Amazon might have figured out how

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.000
to deliver books the fastest,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.060
but they've got nothing on a bookstore

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:19.100
in Philly who delivers books on horseback.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.760
It's amazing and that's how
I wanna receive my books

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.020
from now on.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.970
The even cooler thing
is the story is called

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.400
Harriett's Bookshop named

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.580
after abolitionist Harriet Tubman.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.110
And their mission is to
actually honor the legacy

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:33.180
of black Americans.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.100
Here to tell us more is the
owner of Harriett's Bookshop.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.834
So say hi to Janine who usually watches

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.013
on NBC10 Philadelphia at 2.

00:00:41.013 --> 00:00:43.600
So Janine, so horseback delivery is just

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.090
like one way that your
store is different right?

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:46.923
- Right, right.

00:00:46.923 --> 00:00:49.010
Our store does a lot of
things very differently.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.330
So what you see when
we're delivering books

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.320
by horseback is a part of our mission

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.350
to celebrate Harriet Tubman,

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.480
to celebrate women
authors and women artists

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.760
and women activists.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.680
And what happened was the
Fletcher Street Riding Club

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.597
came together and they were like,

00:01:02.597 --> 00:01:03.650
"How can we support you?"

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.880
Right, so our bookshop had
only been open for six weeks,

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.623
six weeks before the pandemic hit.

00:01:08.623 --> 00:01:09.456
- Oh wow.

00:01:09.456 --> 00:01:12.040
- And so all many, many
communities have come together

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.030
to support us which I think is beautiful.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.357
And what we did was we said,

00:01:15.357 --> 00:01:17.147
"Okay, we're gonna jump on horseback

00:01:17.147 --> 00:01:18.747
"and we're gonna keep on reading.

00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:21.110
"We're gonna keep children
excited about books."

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:23.410
And that's what we've been
doing as much as we can.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:26.209
- What a cool, like
innovative way as well.

00:01:26.209 --> 00:01:27.042
That's so cool.

00:01:27.042 --> 00:01:29.110
- And yeah, so it's been
a way that we can like,

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.240
again, keep it fresh keep it funky,

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.560
keep it exciting for folks

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.393
- And personalize it, yeah.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.870
- And, and now the Bookshop is a whole

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:35.980
nother bookshop again.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.340
Right, so we, we had artists come together

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.920
and when you walk in, you're
literally inside of a book.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.443
So there's illustrations on
every wall, on the floors, yeah.

00:01:44.443 --> 00:01:46.700
- Love that, what a clever
way to get people back

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.330
in stores and buying
like, like reading books.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.610
I like having something
tangible still in my hand.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.443
- Absolutely.

00:01:52.443 --> 00:01:53.560
- I can't, I've tried so hard.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.910
I can't do like the reader thing.

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:55.790
I can't do it.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.250
I like the smell of a book.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.920
I like going into a bookstore.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:01:59.780
I love all of it.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.950
So where did your love
of reading come from?

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.310
- So many places but one
my mother was getting,

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.250
who was a librarian.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.860
She was getting her master's degree when

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.420
I was a little girl.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.300
And as she was doing that,
she started to go blind.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.850
And so what happened was my mother,

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.570
very tenacious woman,
decided to keep on going

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.520
to school and she would have
us read her books to her.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.440
So that's what we did.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.120
We read to her, we wrote with her,

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.867
for her and she continue
until she got that degree.

00:02:24.867 --> 00:02:27.650
And I think that watching
books as a community effort

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.160
in our household became like
a part of my whole life.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.610
- What a special
connection that y'all have.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.810
What a beautiful thing.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:34.830
- Thank you, thank you.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.690
- And just to keep persevering and keep

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.770
and not let that get in your way.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:38.603
- Absolutely.
- Wow.

00:02:38.603 --> 00:02:39.436
Well, thank you so much.

00:02:39.436 --> 00:02:40.596
I love,

00:02:40.596 --> 00:02:41.429
you have a powerful story.
- Thank you.

00:02:41.429 --> 00:02:42.262
- I love this book store.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.180
Everybody go visit.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.390
I'm liking your post, right now.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.296
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:02:46.296 --> 00:02:48.160
And that's not all.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.800
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen makers of G2,

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.360
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.050
want to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you ma'am,

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.950
so they are going to
be writing you a check

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.600
for $1,000 just to help out.
- (laughing) Thank you.

00:03:01.087 --> 00:03:02.160
- Thank you so much.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.367
And you look so beautiful and cool.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.367
I'm so jealous right now of this outfit.

